{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-163030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/ca0ff396606039accf8c3acb4fd1b8e505dd16d2fe9b765fcd5c043d1538a573.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{kg}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\,\\text{kg}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}+1,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+x]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =({2}^{3}+2)-({1}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163013" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}\\,\\text{kg}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163013" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\,\\text{kg}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/d64311921135cf8dea0ec70bb0a83909fb1dba52664f4d6080de596be1693d5e.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}8{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-4{x}^{-2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{4}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $3\\,\\text{kg}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "2\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "3\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{kg}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\,\\text{kg}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/d0e2bd46bf7db6e20f321383e8e0440a2a86f263ce5eb256d20db71f5c632e27.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}-10\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}-10,\\,a=2,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}6{x}^{2}-10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{x}^{3}-10x]_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 27-10\\cdot 3)-(2\\cdot 8-10\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $28\\,\\text{kg}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "16\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "20\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "22\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "28\\,\\text{kg}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "28\\,\\text{kg}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/32500120ed36acde90f5b27c44a6cf45f2d4766bacb5eb097debc0cd7117f27f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3{x}^{2}-x,\\,a=1,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}-x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(27-\\frac{9}{2})-(1-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $22\\,\\text{kg}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "18\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "22\\,\\text{kg}"] ["math" "24\\,\\text{kg}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22\\,\\text{kg}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=4-x\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4-x,\\,a=0,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (4-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{2},$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{2},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}-{1}^{4} \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/887bc91e2565fa24630af4cb74b28723783e31f4769495f0a28a622d73d176de.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (6x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =2.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "3.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "4.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3x+1,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot (3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{4}{2})-(1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "6.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=3x.$ Given that the rod's mass is $6$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot 3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{8}{6}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-162957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/887bc91e2565fa24630af4cb74b28723783e31f4769495f0a28a622d73d176de.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=x+{x}^{2}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{5}{6}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x+{x}^{2},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{7}{12})}{(\\frac{5}{6})}=\\frac{7}{10}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{10}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le e$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Given that the rod's mass is $1$ unit, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,a=1,\\,b=e.\n$$\n\nSo, the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{e-1}{1}=e-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2e-1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{e-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{e-1}"] ["math" "e"] ["math" "e-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 4$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=\\sqrt{x}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,a=0,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3/2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\cdot \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot {4}^{5/2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{64}{5})}{(\\frac{16}{3})}=\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-162981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{12}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{64}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-162981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/54e5dd5fdea01c02b968a6040068e190676841cb8d7b7fc05c561e02d522bbf1.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{15}{32}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=4.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4})}{(\\frac{15}{32})}=\\frac{8}{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c823fb7d2cc7468b671d939650b6f66aec8a2ceafacec5f0fa245dcc98fac93b"} {"question" "q-163022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "q-163022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/state.json" "file_sha256" "7ed25c207684a65947b3b5b739e4ff35e728d705267f72a7ac05ab6d02b23734"} {"question" "e-12475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda(x) =2x\\, \\textrm{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/8c8386ff979b46cd994f1ace60f681a6590856e6960e7d74c71a29bb3f0f2d1a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/example-12475.json" "file_sha256" "0960d209ed51f189e73117a559d7af80684767eb7e19b8ebbe947026d24be222"} {"question" "e-12475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b,$ if $\\lambda(x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm = \\int_a^b \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x) = 2x, \\qquad \na=1, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\textrm{kg}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/example-12475.json" "file_sha256" "0960d209ed51f189e73117a559d7af80684767eb7e19b8ebbe947026d24be222"} {"question" "e-12473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = (x+4)\\,\\textrm{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/example-12473.json" "file_sha256" "195d2fe75a7a9f19223802ca82107071db78fa568ff20c1a3b90e68401911f4f"} {"question" "e-12473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda(x)$ for $a \\leq x \\leq b$ is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_a^b x\\, \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x+4, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}+4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot {3}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $27\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot \\textrm{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/example-12473.json" "file_sha256" "195d2fe75a7a9f19223802ca82107071db78fa568ff20c1a3b90e68401911f4f"} {"question" "e-12474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/assets/461c4cb760541ea435620803689e193d13c9cb4706a59b031d37da6ffd49ab9f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = x^3.$ Given that the rod's mass is $4$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/example-12474.json" "file_sha256" "d89294624e6682df5cb38a7aedea22d96e24f9ae33fee58bda86ebfea308b69e"} {"question" "e-12474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda(x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\int_a^b \\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\int_a^b \\, x\\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x^3, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=2.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(32-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x}= \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{32}{5}\\right)}{4} = \\dfrac{8}{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that this result makes intuitive sense. Since $\\lambda$ is an increasing function of $x,$ we would expect the center of mass to be located closer to the right endpoint and further from the left endpoint." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/example-12474.json" "file_sha256" "d89294624e6682df5cb38a7aedea22d96e24f9ae33fee58bda86ebfea308b69e"} {"question" "q-162948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040800/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "65274e2d6b9c4bd9bcb7cf1c8e617f0769ac1912e84810e9e5cac166811531bf" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "The moment is ∫₁² xλ(x)dx=∫₁²4x³dx=[x⁴]₁²=16−1=15 kg·m. This establishes original option c and agrees with the authentic worked solution, stored key, and saved Correct grading. Bare kg and m in the legacy value denote the same units as the captured styled text." "bindings" {"problem" "473fdef2b0f731712547b6c7fc28be745b708901074a71cc048f883747c08232" "worked_solution" "c1a96ee0efbc609f55f660d316688962153ea65a2545c776b